{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800568-indomitable-vs-vinculum","id":800568,"title":"Indomitable vs. Vinculum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T07:27:52-08:00","id":800568,"title":"Indomitable vs. Vinculum","content":"I did a search. Found nothing.<br /> <br /> Should Indomitable apply against Vinculum?<br /> <br /> Either:<br /> The Vinculum roll itself<br /> The addiction roll to Vitae<br /> or rolls where the Regnant is trying to use the Vinculum to aid persuasion rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T07:41:50-08:00","id":800574,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Sure, why not to the first? Its a crap roll to begin with, and gets only harder with more blood fed. Its not quite a power, but I'd allow it. I also allow it against rolling against the Kiss. <br /> <br /> No to addiction. That's not supernatural mind compulsion - that's a very natural addiction to the rush of life energy.<br /> No to Regent, since that's more mundane rolls - all the supernatural mind control that's going to happen has happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-04-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T07:44:04-08:00","id":800576,"title":"","content":"1. I'd say definitely, it is supernatural base emotion manipulation, which is pretty much what Indomitable is for.<br /> <br /> 2. Now this is a lot sketchier. It could be argued that even this is magic, but I've always felt that this part is pretty mundane. It's an addictive drug.<br /> <br /> 3. And it becomes sketchier still. As such, I don't know, I'd have to think about it more heavily. It's still manipulating your emotions, and it is still supernatural, so I want to say yes, but it really is a border case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T10:15:14-08:00","id":800626,"title":"","content":"1. Indomitable is mortal/ghoul only and they expressly don't get to roll to resist vinculum, so no. <br /> 2 and 3 I would say yes since both are supernatural in origin. A regnant doesn't get to opt out of using the vinculum modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T10:39:24-08:00","id":800638,"title":"","content":"It's Weakened Bond that is mortal/ghoul only, though frankly I think Elders should be able to have that merit as well. Indomitable is available to anyone with at least three dots of Resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 01-04-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T11:22:56-08:00","id":800656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800568-indomitable-vs-vinculum?p=800626#post800626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Indomitable is mortal/ghoul only and they expressly don't get to roll to resist vinculum, so no.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually is not. It is even reprinted in VtR 2e, not just GMC/CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:42:31-08:00","id":800882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800568-indomitable-vs-vinculum?p=800656#post800656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually is not. It is even reprinted in VtR 2e, not just GMC/CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't matter really. Most things don't get to roll to resist vinculum and since there's no innate victim resistance for the potential regnant to have to roll overcome, the merit wouldn't apply. If it's a case of a vinculum being established on another vampire, I'd say it may apply only if said vampire is spending the willpower to make an active attempt to resist the establishment of a vinculum stage. But even that's somewhat sketchy because one, resisting the vinculum is a matter of one's innate blood concentration (which is easily diluted), not a measurement of their mental fortitude. Two, vinculums tend to form automatically as a side effect of consuming kindred blood but the act of blood tasting (not vinculum establishment) can be used to create other effects or used to boost the effectiveness of other powers that don't involve mental or emotional coercion, which is when the merit <u>is</u> applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-04-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:47:23-08:00","id":801354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800568-indomitable-vs-vinculum?p=800882#post800882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter really.</div> </div> </div> </div> Lets not confuse the issue; everyone should agree that vampires can take Indomitable. Its in the vampire book, in the section of merits vampires can take, and without the Mortal Only tag that some merits in the book have. This is important to establish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even that's somewhat sketchy because one, resisting the vinculum is a matter of one's innate blood concentration (which is easily diluted), not a measurement of their mental fortitude. </div> </div> </div> Indomitable is resistance to supernatural powers, not general mental fortitude. The merit specifically calls out that it does not apply to any mundane attempts; if it was mental fortitude, then it would apply to people trying to persuade you, or use drugs on you. It only applies to magic used to manipulate your thoughts/emotions. Its a form of supernatural defense. And you cannot argue that the vinculum isn't a supernatural effect that manipulates your thoughts and emotions. You can argue that the bond is not a -power-, and Indomitable only applies to Disciplines, Devotions, Rites, Rituals, Gifts, Arcana, etc as proper powers. But you can't argue that Indomitable is just mental fortitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two, vinculums tend to form automatically as a side effect of consuming kindred blood but the act of blood tasting (not vinculum establishment) can be used to create other effects or used to boost the effectiveness of other powers that don't involve mental or emotional coercion, which is when the merit <u>is</u> applicable. </div> </div> </div> Citation? Examples? The only power in Requiem 2e that I see that doesn't establish a blood bond when it includes drinking vitae is the Ordo Dracul Blood Cleansing Ritual Scale. And the whole point of that ability is to remove blood bonds. There are two Oaths, a Protean 1 ability and a Cruac ritual that let you absorb or drink vitae without fear of a vinculum, but that's establishing a mystical defense. The Lying Mind can include feeding vitae to the victim, but at no point does it suggest the lack of a blood bond forming, especially since you can put the vitae on the person's forehead instead. You might argue that Hydra's Vitae shouldn't establish a blood bond, but it doesn't say it specifically. Undead Menses, the only way I know to boost the effectiveness of other powers with spilled vitae, doesn't require tasting, just touching.<br /> <br /> Care to back up your claim? I don't see any evidence of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T11:58:59-08:00","id":801537,"title":"","content":"Indomitable applies to contested rolls against mind altering supernatural effects.<br /> <br /> Is the bond a mind altering supernatural effect? Yes<br /> <br /> Therefore, indomitable applies to any contested rolls that the bond calls for. The bond calls for a roll if a vampire spends a point of willpower. Therefore, Indomitable applies to that roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T05:38:35-08:00","id":802009,"title":"","content":"Seems like most agree it should apply to resisting Vinculum. I agree, but I wasn't sure; very few things seem to help against Vinculum. Not quite so much consensus on the other two. I probably wouldn't do addiction, at least. Given that the first stage of blood bond is only a +1, the -2 from Indomitable would make it easier to resist Stage One Blood Bond than if someone didn't have any Vinculum at all. So I guess it probably shouldn't work for that, either.<br /> <br /> Thank you, everyone, for the interesting discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:28:34-08:00","id":802167,"title":"","content":"There is a certain amusement value to be had from someone who's thoroughly blood bound, but stubbornly insistent that they know what's best better than you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:23:55-08:00","id":802427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800568-indomitable-vs-vinculum?p=802167#post802167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a certain amusement value to be had from someone who's thoroughly blood bound, but stubbornly insistent that they know what's best better than you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The third stage of vinculum alludes to thralls who would mess stuff up for their regnant only for the degree of attention it brings to them from their object of desire. Hence why a wise Kindred might refrain from the practice. Could be very well playing with fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}